# Beats — inside the Internet (the cells + the way out)
#
# These play to a captured guest. Hacker_Zero arms; The_Banned warns. Each
# gates on `guest.captured` so it reads differently to the free. The Sysadmin
# interrogation and the Firewall now live *on their props* as owned beats
# (see `cast/algorithm.loom`), reached by `-> self.interrogation` /
# `-> self.firewall` — the scene sits beside the scan that triggers it.

# Hacker_Zero arms a captive instead of saving them. `SELF` resolves to
# whichever prop routed here (Hacker_Zero), so the booth needn't restate it.
== hacker_tool(guest)
  cast: Hacker_Zero, guest
  SELF
    The Glitchers don't break you out. We hand you the tools and you walk yourself out.
    Take this — a one-time heat-sink. Burns your trail clean.
  * Take the heat-sink
    <set: guest.heat = 0>
    <broadcast: cloaked to participant(guest)>
  * Ask about the firewall
    The Oracle knows where it's thin. Stay cold, and run when the lights go out.
    <set: guest.karma += 5>

# The Banned — a ghost nobody could log out.
== banned_ghost(guest)
  cast: The_Banned, guest
  SELF
    <after: guest.captured>
      I've been in here since the old forums. Permabanned. No appeal, no escape.
      Don't end up like me. The Glitchers are real. Find the static.
    <otherwise>
      A flickering figure mouths something at you through the glass. You can't quite read it.
